Short:        Unreal MiniGL for AmigaOS 68k
Author:       Amiga 68k / MiniGL port by arczi84; based on UE1 ports by Northfear, BSzili and BeWorld
Type:         Games/Shoot3D
Version:      1.4.1
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.x, 68060-compatible CPU with FPU, RTG, MiniGL/PiStorm3D, AHI
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

Unreal MiniGL is an AmigaOS 68k port of Unreal Engine 1.
This package uses game data from the Unreal S3 OEM v219 release.
The engine is based on the v200 source with Amiga and MiniGL modifications;
v219 refers to the game data, not a replacement v219 engine source tree.

The inspected S3 OEM v219 disc contains Core.u, Engine.u, Fire.u and
UnrealI.u matching the original retail v200 reference byte-for-byte.
The port's modified packages and configuration are applied over the data.
Unreal Gold, Unreal Tournament and patched 224/226/227 installations are
not supported by this package. Do not mix their files with this installation.


Installing the v219 data again:
------------------------------

For a fresh installation, run from the package drawer:

  Execute Download-and-Install

This downloads and mounts the S3 OEM v219 ISO, then runs Install-Data-219.
Networking and C:UnZip are required. Wget and ImageMount are included.
For an already mounted disc, run:

  Execute Install-Data-219

The installer refuses to overwrite an installation containing System/Engine.u.
See INSTALL-219.txt for manual paths, disk/RAM requirements and mount details.
INSTALACJA-219.txt contains the Polish instructions.
Install-Data and INSTALL-200.txt describe the separate retail v200 disc route;
use Install-Data-219 for the S3 OEM v219 disc used by this package.

Updating from 1.3 or 1.4:
-------------------------

Only the executable changed. Unpack Tools/Unreal-MiniGL.zip over your
Unreal drawer (it contains System/Unreal-MiniGL). Your Unreal-MiniGL.ini is
kept. When updating from 1.2, also set UseWindowBrightness=True in
[NMiniGLDrv.NMiniGLRenderDevice] to use the new brightness.

Saves made with older versions may carry state written by the old
executable (for example glitched movers or ice textures). If something
looks wrong after loading an old save, continue from a new save.

Changes in 1.4.1:
-----------------

- Fixed the hang/crash when entering Rrajigar Depths (Dug), Ruins and NaliC
  on installations that do have Editor.u (it is on the game discs): the
  editor package needs native classes from UnrealEd (e.g. Editor.TransBuffer)
  that this port does not have. The Amiga build now always skips it; the
  maps only reference stray editor textures from it.
- F10 exit: the fullscreen game screen is moved to the back before MiniGL
  frees its buffers, so the last frame no longer shows shifted upwards.
- The executable identifies itself as Unreal-MiniGL 1.4.1.

Changes in 1.4:
---------------

- Fixed the hang when leaving Rrajigar Mine for Rrajigar Depths (Dug), and
  the same problem in Ruins and NaliC: these maps reference editor-only
  textures from Editor.u, which is missing from some installations. Missing
  import packages are now logged and ignored instead of stopping the load.
- Fixed ice/glass textures (IceTexture, e.g. in TerraLift): their settings
  were read 2 bytes off on 68k, so they used invalid texture pointers and
  did not animate.
- The Workbench pointer no longer appears over the menus while the game
  window has focus (also in fullscreen).
- Fixed C++ error handling in the 68k build (built without
  -ffunction-sections), so a missing file is reported instead of crashing.
- The executable identifies itself as Unreal-MiniGL 1.4.

Changes in 1.3:
---------------

- Fixed key mapping: Shift, Alt and Ctrl no longer show up as F20-F24.
  Caps Lock, Help, minus, apostrophe, Pause and the Amiga numeric keypad
  are now mapped.
- Removed the stray class name beside Start Game and the stray value beside
  Prioritize Weapons. Hid Advanced Options, which has no panel in this port.
- The music volume slider now works while a song is playing.
- Fixed starting a new game when the maps are not next to the System drawer
  (e.g. Paths on volumes such as UEGame:Maps/*.unr). The configured Paths
  are now read correctly.
- Brightness now scales the lighting linearly, like the software renderer,
  instead of a gamma curve that tinted whole rooms. Works on both PiStorm3D
  and Classic/QuarkTex and is enabled by default (UseWindowBrightness=True,
  Brightness=0.5).
- A crash no longer takes down the whole system: the game removes its mouse
  input handler, logs the error to Unreal.log and exits.

Changes in 1.2:
---------------

- Fixed assigning Space, Enter and letter keys in Customize Controls.
- Removed stray values beside Crosshair and Customize Controls.
- Added brightness correction for PiStorm3D; disabled it on Classic/QuarkTex.
- The executable identifies itself as Unreal-MiniGL 1.2.

Known issues:
-------------

- Changing the player skin in the Player menu has no visible effect.

Requirements:
-------------

- AmigaOS 3.x.
- A 68060-compatible CPU with FPU (including a suitable PiStorm setup).
- MiniGL.library v29.1 for Pistorm 3D/Classic. WinUAE with QuarkTex.
- Configured AHI for sound.

Configuration:
--------------

Edit Unreal/System/Unreal-MiniGL.ini. The active renderer is:

[Engine.Engine]
GameRenderDevice=NMiniGLDrv.NMiniGLRenderDevice
WindowedRenderDevice=NMiniGLDrv.NMiniGLRenderDevice
RenderDevice=NMiniGLDrv.NMiniGLRenderDevice

This package starts in a 640x480 window. Change ViewportX, ViewportY and
StartupFullscreen in [NSDLDrv.NSDLClient] to adjust the display settings.
Automatic timedemo is disabled (AutoTimedemo=False).
Sound is enabled (UseSound=True); SoundDrv.NullAudioSubsystem is the name
of this port's SDL/AHI audio driver, despite the word "Null" in its name.

MiniGL renderer notes and limitations:
-------------------------------------

- This port uses the fixed-function NMiniGLDrv renderer. The MorphOS TinyGL
  and GLES/shader renderer requirements do not apply to this package.
- The MiniGL path in the port currently forces UseMultiTexture=False,
  UseBGRA=False and UseHwPalette=False. Setting them to True in the INI
  does not enable these features in this path. These are port restrictions,
  not a claim that every MiniGL version lacks the corresponding features.
- DetailTextures=False and NoFiltering=True are the supplied defaults.
- Brightness scales the lightmaps linearly (0.5 = original look, 1.0 =
  lighting x1.5). UseWindowBrightness=True enables it (the default in this
  package); False ignores the Brightness setting.
- Per-texture filter cache (mglfiltercache) is always enabled.
- No numeric texture-size, texture-memory or other GL limits have been
  verified for the user's installed MiniGL/backend. Do not assume that
  TinyGL limits also apply to MiniGL. Actual limits depend on that backend
  and need to be checked on the target system.


